3. Method and data

The method follows ChatTS (Xie et al., "ChatTS: Aligning Time Series with LLMs via Synthetic Data for Enhanced
Understanding and Reasoning", arXiv:2412.03104). No ChatTS code or weights are included.

Training used the ChatTS synthetic training data (https://huggingface.co/datasets/ChatTSRepo/ChatTS-Training-Dataset),
windows of real series from TSB-AD-U (https://github.com/TheDatumOrg/TSB-AD) and prompts from databricks-dolly-15k
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/databricks/databricks-dolly-15k). None of these datasets is redistributed here.

The real series were gathered by TSB-AD from their original sources. Those used in training, with their licences as
stated by each source: the MIT-BIH Supraventricular Arrhythmia, Long-Term ECG and Arrhythmia databases of PhysioNet
(Open Data Commons Attribution License v1.0); OPPORTUNITY and Daphnet of the UCI Machine Learning Repository and
CATS (CC BY 4.0); the Server Machine Dataset of OmniAnomaly (MIT); Exathlon (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0); WSD, SED and Power
(no licence stated).
